====================================================
            LINUX FILE PERMISSIONS
====================================================

CHECK PERMISSIONS
-----------------
ls -l                  Long listing
ll                     Long listing

FILE TYPES
----------
-                      Regular file
d                      Directory
l                      Symbolic link

PERMISSION CLASSES
------------------
u                      User/Owner
g                      Group
o                      Others
a                      All

PERMISSION VALUES
-----------------
r = 4                  Read
w = 2                  Write
x = 1                  Execute

PERMISSION COMBINATIONS
-----------------------
--- = 0
--x = 1
-w- = 2
-wx = 3
r-- = 4
r-x = 5
rw- = 6
rwx = 7

FILE PERMISSIONS
----------------
r                      Read content
w                      Modify content
x                      Execute file

DIRECTORY PERMISSIONS
---------------------
r                      List contents
w                      Create/Delete files
x                      Enter directory (cd)

CHANGE PERMISSION
-----------------
chmod 755 file
chmod 644 file
chmod 777 file

SYMBOLIC METHOD
---------------
chmod u+r file         Add read to user
chmod g+w file         Add write to group
chmod o+x file         Add execute to others

chmod u-r file         Remove read from user
chmod g-w file         Remove write from group

chmod u=rwx file       Set exact permission
chmod a=rwx file       Set permission for all

COMMON PERMISSIONS
------------------
777                    rwxrwxrwx
755                    rwxr-xr-x
750                    rwxr-x---
744                    rwxr--r--
700                    rwx------
666                    rw-rw-rw-
644                    rw-r--r--
600                    rw-------

UMASK
-----
umask                  Check umask
umask 022              Set umask

Maximum File Permission      = 666
Maximum Directory Permission = 777

DEFAULT PERMISSION
------------------
Maximum Permission - UMASK

umask 022
File:       666 - 022 = 644
Directory:  777 - 022 = 755

umask 002
File:       666 - 002 = 664
Directory:  777 - 002 = 775

OWNERSHIP
---------
chown user file
                       Change owner

chown user:group file
                       Change owner and group

chown :group file
                       Change group

chown -R user:group dir
                       Recursive ownership

chgrp group file
                       Change group

chgrp -R group dir
                       Recursive group change
====================================================
